Legacy Linux database backup helper

The Linux scripts remain inputs to the legacy native installer in build.sh.
They dump the clinlims PostgreSQL schema, compress it, retain local copies and
send queued copies to their configured FTP destination. They do not back up
installation keys, certificates or Docker configuration.

The obsolete HTTP upload receiver and its Windows/Haiti upload scripts have
been removed. Sites that deployed copies must remove the CGI endpoint from
their web server and replace the old upload destination. Removing repository
files does not change those deployed copies or delete their existing backups.
Repository history retains the removed code.
